@@ -50,9 +50,15 @@ The six operations are `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`. Pa
 - Invalid patches and failing operations throw a `JsonPatchError`, which is exported too. A pointer error inside an
   operation is reported as a `JsonPatchError` whose `cause` is the `JsonPointerError`.
 - `add` into an object replaces an existing member; `add` into an array inserts at the index, and `-` appends.
-- `move` cannot move a value into one of its own children. `remove` cannot remove the whole document.
+- `move` cannot move a value into one of its own children. `remove` cannot remove the whole document, so `move` cannot
+  take the whole document either.
 - `test` compares JSON values: object members match in any order, array elements in order.
-- An operation without a `value` (or a `from`, for `move` and `copy`) is invalid. `undefined` is not a JSON value and
-  is rejected as a value.
+- An operation without a `value` (or a `from`, for `move` and `copy`) is invalid. Every `value` must be a JSON value:
+  `null`, a boolean, a finite number, a string, an array, or an object with a plain prototype, all of whose members are
+  JSON values. `undefined`, `NaN`, infinities, functions, symbols, bigints, `Date`s, `Map`s, class instances and cyclic
+  structures are rejected, at any depth.
+- Every `path` and `from` is parsed when the patch is checked, so a malformed pointer in any operation rejects the whole
+  patch before any operation runs. Its error is a `JsonPatchError` whose `cause` is the `JsonPointerError`.
+- A patch that is not an array, or that has a hole in it, is rejected with a `JsonPatchError`.
 
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
